# Copy to scripts/exhibit.env and edit. The copy is not in git, because every machine's
# port and certificate paths are its own and a pull must never overwrite them.
# install-service.sh makes that copy for you if there isn't one.
#
# Plain KEY=value, no quotes, no `export`.

# 80 is what makes the address plain http://sharedsky with no port after it. Binding it as a
# non-root user is what AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE in the unit file is for.
SKY_PORT=80

# Serve http rather than TLS.
#
# Read this before leaving it on: the camera only works in a secure context, and plain http
# is not one. The gallery and admin screens have no camera and are perfectly happy here; the
# visitor interaction is not, and on the tablet it needs either the browser flag described in
# the README or a certificate below.
SKY_HTTP=1

# For https instead: delete SKY_HTTP above, set SKY_PORT=443, and point these at a
# certificate issued for the *name* clients type — one for an IP address will not do.
# SKY_CERT=/etc/ssl/sharedsky/sharedsky.crt
# SKY_KEY=/etc/ssl/sharedsky/sharedsky.key
